  "Question": "If \\(A\\) is a subset of \\(B\\), which of the following statements must be true?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Every element of \\(B\\) is in \\(A\\)",
    "B": "\\(A\\) has fewer elements than \\(B\\)",
    "C": "Every element of \\(A\\) is in \\(B\\)",
    "D": "\\(A\\) cannot equal \\(B\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The definition of a subset is that every element of \\(A\\) is an element of \\(B\\). The set \\(A\\) can equal \\(B\\), so it does not necessarily have fewer elements.",
